{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayFaithful","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayFaithful","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealLimitTransfer"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthdayFaithful_independent_witnessed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthdayFaithful_independent_witnessed","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BirthdayFaithful.lean#L135-L154","doc":"**Independence, with the two halves actually joined.**\n\n⚠ The conjunction above is **weaker than its name**, and the gap is easy to miss. Its first\nconjunct says *some* `SurrealField` structure exists on `ℝ*`; its second says `flatBirthday`\nfails the mixin. Nothing in the statement says these concern the **same** structure — read\nliterally it would be satisfied by an unrelated witness for each half, which is not\nindependence.\n\nThis is the honest form: **one** structure, satisfying all six axioms, whose *own* birthday\nfails the mixin. It is what the earlier docstring already claimed (\"witnessed by\n`flatBirthday` on `ℝ*`\") and what the conjunction did not say.\n\nThe proof is unchanged because `surrealFieldHyperreal.birthday` **is** `flatBirthday` by\ndefinition — so the content was always there, and only the statement was loose. That is\nprecisely why it was worth tightening rather than leaving as a comment: a reader checking\nthe theorem, not the field assignment, could not have known. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:birthday-axioms-do-not-pin-the-birthday","label":"thm:birthday-axioms-do-not-pin-the-birthday","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/birthday-axioms-do-not-pin-the-birthday.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthdayFaithful_independent_of_surrealField_axioms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthdayFaithful_independent_of_surrealField_axioms","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BirthdayFaithful.lean#L127-L133","doc":"**Summary, as a single statement.**  The six birthday axioms are satisfiable together\nwith the *negation* of the mixin — witnessed by `flatBirthday` on `ℝ*` — so the mixin adds\nstrictly new content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.flatBirthday_not_faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.flatBirthday_not_faithful","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BirthdayFaithful.lean#L110-L125","doc":"**The flat model fails the mixin**, at `n = 2`.\n\n`flatBirthday` assigns `1` to every nonzero element, so `flatBirthday (2 : ℝ*) = 1 ≠ 2`.\nSince `flatBirthday` *does* satisfy all six birthday axioms\n(`HyperrealLimitTransfer.surrealFieldHyperreal`), this shows `BirthdayFaithful` is **not\nderivable** from them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_natCast_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_natCast_eq","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BirthdayFaithful.lean#L100-L103","doc":"With the mixin, the two halves meet: the bound of §1 is attained. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayFaithful.birthday_natCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayFaithful.birthday_natCast","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BirthdayFaithful.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Conway: the natural number `n` is born on day `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayFaithful.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayFaithful.mk","kind":"ctor","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BirthdayFaithful.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayFaithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayFaithful","kind":"class","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BirthdayFaithful.lean#L86-L98","doc":"**`BirthdayFaithful`** — the one equation the six `SurrealField` axioms cannot supply:\nthe natural numbers are born on the day their value names.\n\nA **mixin**, deliberately.  `SurrealField` is used across ~38 modules and most of them do\nnot reason about birthdays; requiring this of all of them would be noise.  Carrying it\nseparately also makes the dependency legible — a result that needs genuine birthday\ncontent takes `[BirthdayFaithful K]`, and one that does not, does not.\n\nCombined with `birthday_natCast_le` (§1, which needs no mixin) this pins `birthday n`\nexactly; the mixin supplies only the half that was missing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_natCast_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_natCast_le","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BirthdayFaithful.lean#L67-L82","doc":"**`birthday (n : K) ≤ n`, from the existing axioms.**\n\nInduction: `birthday (n+1) ≤ birthday n ♯ birthday 1 = birthday n ♯ 1 = succ (birthday n)`,\nand `succ` is monotone.  Nothing here needs a new axiom — which is the point. ","signatureChunk":0}]}